soc: sunxi: h713-arisc: crust - which image stays, said in the log

The rules for a crust TF-A started, after review findings K10, K12 and
K13 (07.10.2026):

- A crust is alive when its heartbeat moves within 100 ms. The probe
  sampled 5 ms, half of what TF-A waits; a main loop pass that took
  longer made the driver reset a working crust under the display MIPS.

- A missing file no longer costs HDMI when TF-A's crust runs and its page
  is one this driver reads: the crust is kept, with a warning that names
  the file and the build. Nothing can load that crust again.

- A vendor file that replaces a running crust says so, with the build it
  replaces. That is what happens when the FIT carries crust and the
  board's firmware-name still names the vendor image.

- A kept crust whose handshake is done - an earlier probe took the
  notify, and crust sends no second one - skips the 3 s wait for it.

The crust file the module names is hy310-crust.bin, the HY310's
firmware-name[0]; the board file decides which image is loaded.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
